  "title": "Debugging and Securing agent developer experiences on Windows",
  "description": "This session demonstrates agent developer experiences on Windows. Using live code, we expose Windows capabilities and trace how it is packaged, trusted, and executed by the platform. You will learn how Windows enforces security and lifecycle boundaries, what responsibilities stay with the developer, and how to debug common failure modes such as denied access and misconfiguration.\n\nSeating for this session is first-come, first-served. Add it to your schedule to plan your day and arrive early to secure a spot.",
